<!--
  Real San Jose-area RSS feed: San Jose Jazz, https://www.sanjosejazz.org/events/feed/
  (also a WordPress "The Events Calendar" feed). Same transcription note as
  the other two fixtures: confirmed live via this session's web-fetch tool
  on 2026-10-19 and reconstructed here (sandbox egress can't curl
  sanjosejazz.org directly).

  Why this one is here and marked "do not enable yet" in PREP-NEXT-WEEK.md:
  on the live feed, <pubDate> is clearly the WordPress POST's last-modified
  time, not the show's date. Three real items in a row went
  13 Aug 2026 -> 24 Sep 2026 -> 13 Aug 2026 again, and a fourth, "Legally
  Blue", was dated 07 Feb 2025 despite being listed as upcoming alongside
  2026 shows. A feed that behaves like this will feed wrong dates into the
  engine if it's trusted the way sjsu_calendar.rss.xml and cdm_events.rss.xml
  are. This adapter has no way to detect that from a single item, so the
  fixture's job is to prove the adapter still does the one safe thing: parse
  <pubDate> exactly as given (it has no way to know it's "wrong" here), and
  skip only the one item below with no <pubDate> at all.
-->
